WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you were mayor of
San Antonio.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.937 line:92%
You were Secretary of Housing.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I was.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now you are
running for President.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.640 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It is a crowded field.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.842 line:92%
I don't need to tell you.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
You maybe don't have as much
name recognition

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
as some of the candidates,
and on top of that all,

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
people often confuse you
with your twin.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're really encouraging m
tonight, Seth.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're really encouraging me
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, on top of
everything else --

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:21.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Feel better about myself
already.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you have a twin brother
who's a congressman.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.224 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:28.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so, I imagine that,
you know, just like any twin

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:31.531
that probably gets in the way of
name recognition as well.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.532 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's true.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.200 line:92%
You know, about two months ago

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
he grew a beard so that people
could tell us apart.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:39.472 size:78% position:39%
And then he realized
that it looked so bad

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:43.710
that it wasn't worth it, and h
shaved like four weeks later

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
He likes to go around
telling people

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.279 line:92%
that the way to tell us apar

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that I'm one minute
uglier than he is.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's very nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.419 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You had been mayor

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:55.555
when you got tapped by
the Obama administration.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:56.723 line:92%
And President Obama called you

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
to ask you to be
the Secretary of Housing.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.693
What was that like to get
a phone call like that?

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:05.999
-He did. In fact, I remember
that it was on April 16, 2014.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:08.835
And I remember because
I had just driven through

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:12.338
the drive-through at
Panda Express when he called me.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:12.872 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:16.209
And you know how on your phone
it says unknown or blocked call.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:16.876 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It said, "private."

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
So for all of you,
if you ever get a phone call

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
that says, "private,"
answer the phone.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:22.615 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hopefully I'll be the one
on the other end of the line

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.519 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, there you go.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.520 line:92%
Did you tell him when he calle

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you had just gotten
Panda Express?

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:30.223 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, no.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.192
I think I pretended like I was
behind my mayoral office desk.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Oh, I'm still working
at 9:00 at night."

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.796
-You're, like, yelling at people
who aren't there.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "I'll deal with that
later!"

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had a background
in housing.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was one of the reason
that he tapped you.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:47.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a policy issue
that you had spent years on.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously we referenced it
earlier in the show.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:55.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ben Carson, obviously
a very gifted neurosurgeon

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:57.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that is different
than housing.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.987
How -- What is it like to have
had that position and look a

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:04.924
someone who doesn't seem to have
the same outlook on it?

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:08.495
-Well, I mean, his hearing
yesterday was like watchin

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:13.733
a slow-motion train wreck
until they got to the Oreo part.

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.502 line:92%
And then it was like, "Oh, man."

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:16.636 line:92%
What do you say about that

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:19.506
I was telling some folks
yesterday, that it was --

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
this was one of
the classic cases of,

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It would be funny
if it weren't so sad."

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.279
-Well, that I think the sad part
is again -- because, you know,

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:29.315
obviously different parties ar
going to have different outlooks

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
on how to handle issues
in this country.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:35.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it seems as though
his position is just disdain

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the idea of the government
providing housing

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:39.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
to those who need it.
-Yeah, I mean, what I disagree

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:42.562
with him on is that he seems
to think that if you're poor

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there's something wrong
with you.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.032 line:92%
And I completely reject that

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
HUD serves a lot of people

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.202 line:92%
who are trying their best.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of folks
who are working hard.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.372 line:92%
And just because you're poor

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:54.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
doesn't mean that
something's wrong with you

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:57.710
-You know, I think we've noticed
it amongst many of

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
the candidates who have
thrown their hat in the ring

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.382
Trying to find a signature
issue, trying to find a thin

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:04.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
to let people know how you
might be different than others

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:11.257
Immigration seems to be what
you are staking as your issue.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, you come from
a border state.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.594 line:92%
What about immigration is

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
different as far as
how you see it?

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:19.766
-Well, I think in Texas, you
know, we know that the peopl

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are trying to
come to our border,

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are fleeing
desperate circumstances,

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:26.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
are not a national-securit
threat.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:26.940 line:92%
They're not somehow evil.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.877
They're here because they want
a better life for themselves

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:31.978 line:92%
and for their little children.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:35.215
And they're like immigrant
who have come to this countr

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.984 size:81% position:41%
over the generations
from different places.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:38.885 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And that this president,

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the very beginning
of his campaign,

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.823
has demonized them and used them
as a scapegoat,

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.457 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and on their backs

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
is basically trying
to get re-elected in 2020.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:50.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I just wanted to put ou
an immigration plan

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
that represents
the complete opposite

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:53.566 line:92%
of what this president doe

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:56.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
and says, "Look, we can have
a border that's secure.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:04:01.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we can be compassionat
instead of cruel."

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:02.609 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:06.479
-I think everyone -- or I should
say, many people are critica

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the Trump administration'
policy

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.250 line:92%
in regards to immigration.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
But obviously, you know,
Barack Obama --

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:15.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, he deported a record
number of people,

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:17.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
